{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWacvyCiqQfyEtvFnSRU", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I built the part and exported it to `submission.step`. It's a tee nut: a thin round flange on top (+Z) with a hollow barrel underneath and a hole running through both. My final render (`preview.png`) matches `composite.png` closely in all four views.\n\n`part.py` draws the cross-section and spins it 360° around the Z axis, which gives one solid. Proportions, taking the flange diameter as 1:\n- **Flange:** diameter 1.0, thickness 0.08\n- **Barrel:** outer diameter 0.4, length 0.5\n- **Through-hole:** diameter 0.27\n\nI estimated these by eye from the renders. My first try had the hole too small (0.2) and the barrel too short (0.45), so I fixed both in a second pass.\n\nTwo problems along the way:\n- My first version joined two separate cylinders, but that crashed in this CadQuery setup. Spinning one cross-section avoids the join.\n- The permission system blocked a `sed` command I used to edit the numbers, so I made that change with the file editor instead."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 612, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11612, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 612}, "output_tokens": 343, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e9d1a249-2422-4824-b18c-f267e44dd0a5", "uuid": "09dfd82d-cf74-4828-9bec-2f6960dee51f", "timestamp": "2026-10-29T13:08:02.385Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWacvecWsKGeJuPPLPk4"}
